{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>When my spirit faints</b> — like <i>a prayer of the afflicted when he faints</i>." "<b>When my spirit faints</b> — I am utterly worn out, and You know the path that I desire to walk. R. Moses the Cohen said: <i>נתיבתי</i> (my path) is straight before You, and he did not use the concealers, like <i>אשר ילדה אותה</i> (who bore her)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 142, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:30.907014767Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}